{"providerCalls": 0, "taskWrites": 0, "rawResponsesUnchanged": true, "results": {"critique": {"partial": true, "rejections": [{"summary": "剪枝的重要性分数依赖训练视图的射线相交计数、体积和透明度，且体积经90%分位数归一化，但仍可能偏向背景或大体积高斯，存在误剪细节的风险；单独剪枝会降低质量，需要联合微调（co-adaptation）部分恢复，而恢复仅在训练视图邻域进行，泛化到未覆盖视角存疑。", "reason": "比较数字缺少逐项实验条件，已停止发布。"}], "claims": [{"summary": "Mip-NeRF 360 Datasets：在真实世界大规模场景的重新训练基线比较中，LightGaussian的帧率为FPS 237，模型大小压缩比为Size压缩17.38倍，PSNR差异为PSNR下降0.27 dB；说明以轻微质量损失换取高压缩与提速，该证据不覆盖合成对象级场景。（NVIDIA A6000 GPU，基线3D-GS  *  [16]）", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 9: 3D-GS  *  [16] | 144 | 782MB | 27.40 | 0.813 | 0.217 | 106 | 433MB | 23.66 | 0.845 | 0.178"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 10: Ours | 237 | 45MB | 27.13 | 0.806 | 0.237 | 357 | 25MB | 23.44 | 0.832 | 0.202"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * ."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-23", "quote": "All performance evaluations are conducted on an A6000 GPU."}], "section": "weakness"}, {"summary": "球谐降阶依赖教师模型的知识蒸馏，仅在训练视图附近的高斯采样位姿上监督像素强度，因此对偏离训练轨迹的视角的保真度有限；直接消除高阶SH会降低质量，蒸馏只能缓解。VQ仅对低显著性SH系数实施，位置、旋转、缩放、不透明度及高显著性SH保留为float16，这限制了压缩率；若对位置/旋转/缩放等全部元素量化，作者自述会带来显著精度损失，说明该方法依赖相似外观分组假设，对非欧几何属性并不鲁棒。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Supervision is based on the difference in predicted pixel intensities between the two models, with images synthesized at camera positions by sampling around each training view according to a Gaussian distribution:"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-19", "quote": "Our empirical findings indicate that applying quantization across all elements-especially for attributes like position, rotation, and scale-results in significant accuracy losses and a marked reduction in precision when represented discretely."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-19", "quote": "We propose applying VQ to the Spherical Harmonics (SH) coefficients, based on the assumption that a subgroup of 3d Gaussians typically exhibits a similar appearance."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "To preserve essential attributes, including Spherical Harmonics with higher global significance scores, along with Gaussian position, shape, rotation, and opacity, we skip VQ for these elements and store them directly in float16 format."}], "section": "weakness"}], "message": "**部分分析**\n\n推断：Mip-NeRF 360 Datasets：在真实世界大规模场景的重新训练基线比较中，LightGaussian的帧率为FPS 237，模型大小压缩比为Size压缩17.38倍，PSNR差异为PSNR下降0.27 dB；说明以轻微质量损失换取高压缩与提速，该证据不覆盖合成对象级场景。（NVIDIA A6000 GPU，基线3D-GS  *  [16]） [1] [2] [3]\n\n推断：球谐降阶依赖教师模型的知识蒸馏，仅在训练视图附近的高斯采样位姿上监督像素强度，因此对偏离训练轨迹的视角的保真度有限；直接消除高阶SH会降低质量，蒸馏只能缓解。VQ仅对低显著性SH系数实施，位置、旋转、缩放、不透明度及高显著性SH保留为float16，这限制了压缩率；若对位置/旋转/缩放等全部元素量化，作者自述会带来显著精度损失，说明该方法依赖相似外观分组假设，对非欧几何属性并不鲁棒。 [4] [5] [2]\n\n<details>\n<summary>尚待确认</summary>\n\n另有1项判断暂未确认，未纳入本次结论。\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>待核查问题</summary>\n\n- 待核查：合成对象级场景下的压缩比、帧率与质量损失，以及剪枝后未覆盖视角和VQ码书存储开销的定量影响。\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>原文依据</summary>\n\n- [1] “Table row 9: 3D-GS  *  [16] | 144 | 782MB | 27.40 | 0.813 | 0.217 | 106 | 433MB | 23.66 | 0.845 | 0.178”\n- [1] “Table row 10: Ours | 237 | 45MB | 27.13 | 0.806 | 0.237 | 357 | 25MB | 23.44 | 0.832 | 0.202”\n- [2] “For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * .”\n- [3] “All performance evaluations are conducted on an A6000 GPU.”\n- [4] “Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs.”\n- [4] “Supervision is based on the difference in predicted pixel intensities between the two models, with images synthesized at camera positions by sampling around each training view according to a Gaussian distribution:”\n- [5] “Our empirical findings indicate that applying quantization across all elements-especially for attributes like position, rotation, and scale-results in significant accuracy losses and a marked reduction in precision when represented discretely.”\n- [5] “We propose applying VQ to the Spherical Harmonics (SH) coefficients, based on the assumption that a subgroup of 3d Gaussians typically exhibits a similar appearance.”\n- [2] “To preserve essential attributes, including Spherical Harmonics with higher global significance scores, along with Gaussian position, shape, rotation, and opacity, we skip VQ for these elements and store them directly in float16 format.”\n\n</details>"}, "compare": {"partial": true, "rejections": [], "claims": [{"summary": "原始3DGS以较多高斯表示和自适应密度控制换取视觉质量与实时渲染；LightGaussian以全局显著性剪枝和VQ在轻微质量折让下换取更小模型和更高帧率。直接同条件实验数字来自LightGaussian论文中A6000重训的3D-GS*表1。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-9", "quote": "Our results on previously published datasets show that we can optimize our 3D Gaussians from multi-view captures and achieve equal or better quality than the best quality previous implicit radiance field approaches."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * ."}]}, {"summary": "原始3DGS论文自身的速度、存储与质量声明不能与LightGaussian表1中的重训3D-GS*数字进行跨实验排序；可核对定量比较仅限LightGaussian论文A6000表1白名单行。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "The trained synthetic scenes rendered at 180-300 FPS."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * ."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-23", "quote": "All performance evaluations are conducted on an A6000 GPU."}]}, {"summary": "原始3DGS使用各向异性高斯以较少参数建模复杂形状，并在正文中主张优于显式点云方法的紧凑性；该数字不与LightGaussian表1同条件比较。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "We surpass their reported metrics using approximately one-fourth of their point count, resulting in an average model size of 3.8 MB, as opposed to their 9 MB."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian表1显示Ours的Size低于同条件重训3D-GS*；其方法通过剪枝与VQ减少过参数化表示。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 9: 3D-GS  *  [16] | 144 | 782MB | 27.40 | 0.813 | 0.217 | 106 | 433MB | 23.66 | 0.845 | 0.178"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 10: Ours | 237 | 45MB | 27.13 | 0.806 | 0.237 | 357 | 25MB | 23.44 | 0.832 | 0.202"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS声称达到state-of-the-art视觉质量并支持1080p高质量实时视图合成。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-9", "quote": "Our results on previously published datasets show that we can optimize our 3D Gaussians from multi-view captures and achieve equal or better quality than the best quality previous implicit radiance field approaches."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "在LightGaussian同条件表1中，Ours的PSNR/SSIM略低于3D-GS*，LPIPS略高，属于质量上的小幅折让。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 9: 3D-GS  *  [16] | 144 | 782MB | 27.40 | 0.813 | 0.217 | 106 | 433MB | 23.66 | 0.845 | 0.178"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 10: Ours | 237 | 45MB | 27.13 | 0.806 | 0.237 | 357 | 25MB | 23.44 | 0.832 | 0.202"}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS报告其合成场景可高帧率渲染，并强调1080p实时视图合成；但未与LightGaussian同表并列。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "The trained synthetic scenes rendered at 180-300 FPS."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian表1显示Ours的FPS高于同条件3D-GS*；论文自述在FPS、模型大小、质量间取得平衡。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 9: 3D-GS  *  [16] | 144 | 782MB | 27.40 | 0.813 | 0.217 | 106 | 433MB | 23.66 | 0.845 | 0.178"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-38", "quote": "Table row 10: Ours | 237 | 45MB | 27.13 | 0.806 | 0.237 | 357 | 25MB | 23.44 | 0.832 | 0.202"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS通过密集3D高斯、自适应密度控制、各向异性协方差与快速可见性渲染，优先保证表示精度和实时能力。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "First, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Third, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian通过全局显著性剪枝与VQ减少冗余，并以可微微调补偿量化损失，主动用少量质量换取规模和速度。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-15", "quote": "We rank all Gaussians by their global significance scores to quantitatively guide pruning of the lower-ranked Gaussians."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-32", "quote": "Specifically, by assigning a unique code to each Gaussian, we proceed to implement differentiable finetuning using photometric loss, which is similar to the methodology employed in 3D-GS, and optimize all the attributes in conjunction with VQ."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}], "message": "**部分比较**\n\n推断：原始3DGS以较多高斯表示和自适应密度控制换取视觉质量与实时渲染；LightGaussian以全局显著性剪枝和VQ在轻微质量折让下换取更小模型和更高帧率。直接同条件实验数字来自LightGaussian论文中A6000重训的3D-GS*表1。 [1] [2] [3] [4]\n\n推断：原始3DGS论文自身的速度、存储与质量声明不能与LightGaussian表1中的重训3D-GS*数字进行跨实验排序；可核对定量比较仅限LightGaussian论文A6000表1白名单行。 [5] [4] [6]\n\n\n| 维度 | 论文 1 | 论文 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 表示规模与紧凑性 | 原始3DGS使用各向异性高斯以较少参数建模复杂形状，并在正文中主张优于显式点云方法的紧凑性；该数字不与LightGaussian表1同条件比较。 [5] | 推断：LightGaussian表1显示Ours的Size低于同条件重训3D-GS*；其方法通过剪枝与VQ减少过参数化表示。 [7] [3] |\n| 渲染质量 | 原始3DGS声称达到state-of-the-art视觉质量并支持1080p高质量实时视图合成。 [1] [2] | 推断：在LightGaussian同条件表1中，Ours的PSNR/SSIM略低于3D-GS*，LPIPS略高，属于质量上的小幅折让。 [7] |\n| 渲染速度与实时性 | 原始3DGS报告其合成场景可高帧率渲染，并强调1080p实时视图合成；但未与LightGaussian同表并列。 [5] [1] | 推断：LightGaussian表1显示Ours的FPS高于同条件3D-GS*；论文自述在FPS、模型大小、质量间取得平衡。 [7] [4] |\n| 方法层面的取舍机制 | 原始3DGS通过密集3D高斯、自适应密度控制、各向异性协方差与快速可见性渲染，优先保证表示精度和实时能力。 [1] | LightGaussian通过全局显著性剪枝与VQ减少冗余，并以可微微调补偿量化损失，主动用少量质量换取规模和速度。 [3] [8] [9] [10] |\n\n<details>\n<summary>比较范围</summary>\n\n数字绑定仅选取Mip-NeRF360数据集的FPS、Size、PSNR、SSIM、LPIPS列；Tank&Temple组及其他未选行未在本结论中计算，需另行核对后才能外推；LightGaussian表中的基线为重新训练的3D-GS*，与原始3DGS论文自己的硬件和版本可能不同，不能视为同一实验设置下的独立验证。\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>原文依据</summary>\n\n- 论文 1：3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n- 论文 2：LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n- [1] “We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution.”\n- [2] “Our results on previously published datasets show that we can optimize our 3D Gaussians from multi-view captures and achieve equal or better quality than the best quality previous implicit radiance field approaches.”\n- [3] “pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy.”\n- [4] “method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations.”\n- [4] “For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * .”\n- [5] “The trained synthetic scenes rendered at 180-300 FPS.”\n- [5] “In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters.”\n- [6] “All performance evaluations are conducted on an A6000 GPU.”\n- [5] “We surpass their reported metrics using approximately one-fourth of their point count, resulting in an average model size of 3.8 MB, as opposed to their 9 MB.”\n- [7] “Table row 9: 3D-GS  *  [16] | 144 | 782MB | 27.40 | 0.813 | 0.217 | 106 | 433MB | 23.66 | 0.845 | 0.178”\n- [7] “Table row 10: Ours | 237 | 45MB | 27.13 | 0.806 | 0.237 | 357 | 25MB | 23.44 | 0.832 | 0.202”\n- [1] “First, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;”\n- [1] “Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;”\n- [1] “Third, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering.”\n- [8] “We rank all Gaussians by their global significance scores to quantitatively guide pruning of the lower-ranked Gaussians.”\n- [9] “of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation.”\n- [10] “Specifically, by assigning a unique code to each Gaussian, we proceed to implement differentiable finetuning using photometric loss, which is similar to the methodology employed in 3D-GS, and optimize all the attributes in conjunction with VQ.”\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>尚待确认</summary>\n\n另有3项判断暂未确认，未纳入本次结论。\n\n</details>"}}}
